From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 28/39] RunFDTD: no energy schedule without an end criteria

A run with endCriteria = 0 (a fixed number of timesteps) has nothing to stop on, yet its energy was summed every
Nyquist period during the first 60 s: one pass of one thread over both fields, during which the engine waits. With a
Nyquist period of 51 timesteps that was 4-6 % of a run on 3-17 M cells on the Metal diamond engine and about 3 % on
the multithreaded engine. Without an end criteria the energy is now estimated with the progress report only, as in
v0.37.0; --exact-endcriteria still asks for the schedule. The results of a run do not change.

Generated-by: Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 openems.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/openems.cpp b/openems.cpp
index 9fe7210..fd84e0d 100644
--- a/openems.cpp
+++ b/openems.cpp
@@ -1712,7 +1712,10 @@ void openEMS::RunFDTD()
 	// After that only with the wall-clock progress report, which then is a small overshoot
 	// and saves the (full-domain) energy estimates -- unless --exact-endcriteria asks
 	// for a machine-independent stopping point.
-	bool exactEndCrit = (Eng_Ext_SSD==NULL);
+	// A run without an end criteria (endCriteria = 0, a fixed number of timesteps) has nothing to stop on: no schedule,
+	// as in v0.37.0, and the energy only with the progress report. Each estimate is one pass of one thread over both
+	// fields, during which the engine waits (with a Nyquist period of 51 timesteps, 4-6 % of the run on 3-17 M cells).
+	bool exactEndCrit = (Eng_Ext_SSD==NULL) && ((endCrit>0) || m_exactEndCriteria);
 	if (exactEndCrit)
 	{
 		unsigned int endCritInterval = FDTD_Op->GetExcitationSignal()->GetNyquistNum();
